{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1471619-hollow-doors-and-forcing-entrance","id":1471619,"title":"Hollow Doors and Forcing Entrance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-01T14:31:46-08:00","id":1471619,"title":"Hollow Doors and Forcing Entrance","content":"Hi all, curious how you rule on the following questions in your chronicles:<br /> <br /> HOLLOW DOORS?<br /> Hollows are &quot;with few exceptions ... tied to a single, consistent physical entrance into the Hedge ...&quot;. We also know they &quot;normally only have a single exit into the real world&quot; and that a &quot;clever Huntsman waits for a changeling at the Hedge Entrance to her den.&quot; With Hidden Entrance, we know that the singular &quot;entrance evaporates&quot; once everyone is inside. So, for the basic hollow (without any special features), does it have:<br /> 1) a single entrance/exit to the mortal world<br /> 2) a single entrance/exit to the hedge<br /> 3) a single entrance/exit to both the mortal world and the hedge (in other words, the hedge entrance is also a Hedgeway)<br /> 4) one of each (hedgeway &amp; hedge physical door) that are separate?<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to say #2 (single entrance to the hedge) with the understanding that you can turn that door or any other inside the hollow into a Hedgeway with a point of glamour. How do you handle this?<br /> <br /> FORCING ENTRANCE INTO A HOLLOW?<br /> For getting into someone else's hollow, what counts as &quot;forcing&quot; the entrance? I assume that breaking through a wall for example should also count as a forcing entrance (otherwise, Huntsman would never wait), as would picking a lock on a hollow door and other mundane efforts to get inside. <br /> <br /> However, what about using contracts to do it? Hostile Takeover has clear rules and prompts a clash of wills but seems to get around the Wyrd requirement to get into a hollow in the first place. Should other contracts be treated similarly? Here are some ideas: <br /> *an elemental uses Summon The Loyal Servant to create a air/water servant and merges with it to go under the door?<br /> *Changeling Hours/Touch of Wrath, etc. to destroy the door?<br /> *Dance of the Toys to command the door to open?<br /> *Hidden Reality to create another entrance to the hollow?<br /> *Whispers of Morning to move through the walls?<br /> *Mirror Walk to get inside (having touched the mirror before of course)?<br /> <br /> When do such approaches succeed, provoke a clash of wills, or fail outright? <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26661-autumnking","name":"AutumnKing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T11:51:44-08:00","id":1471683,"title":"","content":"For hollow doors, i would exclude 3 and 4, or else the escape route feature would be of little use.<br /> Rules of the merit seems to contradict, i ve had the same doubts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T13:29:10-08:00","id":1471792,"title":"","content":"For your first question, it honestly depends. I\u2019ve always had my Hollow entrances be a two way path between the interior of the Hollow and the door itself, which has to be opened like a Hedgegate, and that I could exit my Hollow and explore the Hedge like one could leave their house. However, it\u2019s also possible the Hollow entrance simply opens onto the grounds of the Hollow, allowing you to enter into it or simply wander off into the Hedge proper. It depends on how you want to go about it.<br /> <br /> As for the rules for forcing an entry into the Hollow, any attempts to breach it are resisted. This includes trying to get in under the door, making another one with Hidden Reality, Whispers of Morning, Mirror Walk, Changeling Hours and so forth. Remember that Hollows exist inside the Hedge, a place so notoriously flexible that even the mere act of making a deal with a Hobgoblin could cause your surrounding to spontaneously change without anyone\u2019s intent. Given that a Hollow has magic to resist entry, it\u2019s really plausible that if you tried to break in with your examples, it could;<br /> -Seal itself so a body of liquid and air couldn\u2019t possibly fit through;<br /> -Cause the door to break down only for another door to be behind it, or for the outer layer of it to peal off like paint while leaving the functionally intact door standing;<br /> -The contract to simply fail because the Clash of Wills failed;<br /> -Create another door, only for that one to follow the same logic as the already existing one and resist the person who made it;<br /> -Whoever uses Whispers of Morning to phase through the wall, only to end up at the other end of the Hollow, as if the two ends were on opposite sides of the same wall;<br /> -Instead of ending up going through the mirror in the Hollow they step right back out of the same mirror they stepped through.<br /> <br /> Simply put, if these kinds of tricks could allow one to beat a Hollow\u2019s defences, why would any Changeling bother with a Hollow when their Keeper could simply and easily slip in, much less any Huntsmen or Hobs who could become ethereal elements. What the Hollow does to protect its owner depends on what the Changeling wants it to do, and what other features it might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T21:07:45-08:00","id":1471824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutumnKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1471619-hollow-doors-and-forcing-entrance#post1471619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HOLLOW DOORS?<br /> Hollows are &quot;with few exceptions ... tied to a single, consistent physical entrance into the Hedge ...&quot;. We also know they &quot;normally only have a single exit into the real world&quot; and that a &quot;clever Huntsman waits for a changeling at the Hedge Entrance to her den.&quot; With Hidden Entrance, we know that the singular &quot;entrance evaporates&quot; once everyone is inside. So, for the basic hollow (without any special features), does it have:<br /> 1) a single entrance/exit to the mortal world<br /> 2) a single entrance/exit to the hedge<br /> 3) a single entrance/exit to both the mortal world and the hedge (in other words, the hedge entrance is also a Hedgeway)<br /> 4) one of each (hedgeway &amp; hedge physical door) that are separate?</div> </div> </div> </div>A normal Hollow is connected to the mortal world through a single consistent physical entrance/exit to the Hedge and has as many or as few portals out of its boundaries as it is constructed to have, and the nature of it as a place within the Hedge with the qualities of a Hollow allows it to resist intrusion in whatever way you can conceive of.<br /> <br /> The Hedge being what it is, hospitality oaths and their foundational concepts probably play a role, since examples of large Hollows include properties with some amount of large open space; it's possible the mist and maze and low draw-distance of the place allows for some shenanigans with a high canopy or impossible spaces to serve as the mechanism for warding off intruders in those cases, assuming the sheer weight of associated Wyrd isn't purely responsible for blocking off attempts to force the door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}